# Patches must keep LF endings on every machine.
#
# `core.autocrlf=true` is set on this Windows box, so a patch committed with LF
# is checked out with CRLF. `git apply` then fails against upstream's LF sources
# with "patch does not apply" - the hunk context no longer matches. That is
# exactly what happened to runtime/docgen-deterministic-fix.patch: it was
# generated from CRLF working-tree files and could not be applied to v0.2.3.
#
# These files are consumed by `git apply` on a different machine, so their bytes
# must be stable. Never normalise them.
*.patch -text
*.diff  -text
